From 6e45a403c4b36480e0dacf384560330b0cf818c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GPTware AI Team <dcmaxhome@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:31:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] MoE coop: counting-sort run table
 (EXL3_MOE_COOP_FAST_RUNS) and split down-stage reduction
 (EXL3_MOE_COOP_SPLIT_B)

EXL3_MOE_COOP_FAST_RUNS=1 builds the per-expert run table of the wide verify window with a counting sort (per-expert
counts, block scans, warp match_any stable ranks) instead of the O(slots^2) rank loop in block 0 of the rotation
kernel: same table, bit-identical outputs, rotation launch 50-60 us -> 8-9 us at 56-64 verify rows.
EXL3_MOE_COOP_SPLIT_B=1 runs the down-stage reduction as its own launch (same body and order; default off, it did
not help end to end). MOE_COOP_B_WN / MOE_COOP_PF / EXL3_MOE_COOP_DBG=4 are bench knobs; defaults unchanged.
